    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Divine Revulsion"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(emotion, fear, mental)\n\nIf a redcap sees a creature brandish a religious symbol of a good deity (which requires an interact action by that creature) or use one to cast a divine spell, the redcap must attempt a DC 19 Will save. It then becomes temporarily immune to all brandished religious symbols for 10 minutes.\n\nCritical Success: The redcap is unaffected.\nSuccess: The redcap is frightened 2.\nFailure: The redcap gains the fleeing condition for 1 round and is frightened 4."
            },
            "id": "2c323d0f-e137-4dee-80ec-ee52488bc4fa",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:25.944969"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Red Cap"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(necromancy, primal)\n\nA redcap's woolen hat is dyed with the blood of its victims.\n\nIf the redcap loses its cap, it no longer benefits from fast healing and takes a \u20134 status penalty to its damage rolls. It can create a new cap in 10 minutes, but that cap doesn't grant its powers until the redcap has turned it red with Blood Soak. A cap has no benefit for creatures other than the redcap who made it."
            },
            "id": "feb1aa1a-e8eb-4be2-a779-68d6c1d8fe5d",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:25.944969"
            }
          }
        }
